6:     """Shear the rectangular input down-left onto a black canvas.
7: 
8:     Input structure
9:     A rectangular grid of colored pixels with no internal empty region to infer.
10: 
11:     Rule
12:     Create a black output with the same height and width W + H - 1, then copy
13:     each input row r unchanged starting at column H - 1 - r.
14: 
15:     Key insight
16:     The colors and row contents are preserved; only the row offsets change so
17:     the left edge forms a descending diagonal.
18:     """
19:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
